Chat Edit: 'Update your imports
Replace all imports like this:

import { supabase } from '@/lib/supabaseClient';


with:

import { supabase } from '@/lib/supabase';


Affected files:

app/auth/login/page.tsx

app/auth/signup/page.tsx

app/auth/page.tsx

app/dashboard/components/Editor.tsx

app/dashboard/notes/NotesClient.tsx

Check tsconfig.json path alias

Make sure you have something like this:

{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "baseUrl": ".",
    "paths": {
      "@/*": ["./*"]
    }
  }
}


This allows @/lib/... to point to your project root.'

Chat Edit: '1️⃣ Tiptap “different instances of a keyed plugin (history$)” error

This happens if:

You re-mount the editor or use the same plugin (like History) multiple times.

Happens often when useEditor is re-called or multiple Editor components mount/unmount during SSR/CSR mismatches.

Fix

Remove duplicate History extensions.

Make sure you don’t re-instantiate the editor inside a render.

Example of SSR-safe useEditor:

const [mounted, setMounted] = useState(false);

useEffect(() => setMounted(true), []);

// create editor only once, on client
const editor = useEditor(
  mounted
    ? {
        extensions: [
          StarterKit, 
          Underline, 
          Image, 
          Link,
          Table.configure({ resizable: true }),
          TableRow,
          TableHeader,
          TableCell,
        ],
        content: note?.content || "<p></p>",
        editorProps: {
          attributes: { class: "prose max-w-none focus:outline-none" },
        },
        immediatelyRender: false,
      }
    : undefined
);


✅ Key points:

Wrap editor creation in mounted so it only exists on client.

Remove History if you re-use StarterKit, because StarterKit already includes History by default.

immediatelyRender: false prevents SSR hydration issues.

2️⃣ UI issues: Dark/Light toggle & profile logo not opening

These are usually caused by:

Components trying to access window or document during SSR

State not persisted properly or JS errors blocking interactivity

Overly complex dashboard JSX causing slow renders

Quick fixes

Wrap any code that uses window / document in useEffect or check typeof window !== "undefined".

For toggles/buttons:

const [darkMode, setDarkMode] = useState(false);

useEffect(() => {
  if (typeof window !== "undefined") {
    document.documentElement.classList.toggle("dark", darkMode);
  }
}, [darkMode]);


For dropdowns (profile menu):

const [profileOpen, setProfileOpen] = useState(false);

return (
  <div className="relative">
    <button onClick={() => setProfileOpen(!profileOpen)}>Profile</button>
    {profileOpen && (
      <div className="absolute top-full right-0 bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 shadow rounded">
        {/* menu items */}
      </div>
    )}
  </div>
);

3️⃣ Performance / “junky” feeling

Avoid rendering heavy components on SSR.

Only mount editors after client ready (mounted state).

Lazy-load large components or AI calls.

Avoid large synchronous operations (like file parsing) blocking UI. Use async/await and loading spinners.'
